WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.260
Our legal design begins with one rule: points, user payments, and prize money must remain separate.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.330
This is a prototype design, not a legal conclusion.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.721
Launch requires country-specific legal review, licenses where required, and confirmed IP rights.

00:00:14.821 --> 00:00:18.101
The first flow is the money paid by users.

00:00:18.131 --> 00:00:23.553
The planned animation artwork package costs three thousand yen and includes five digital pieces.

00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:29.396
That payment buys the support product. It does not buy competition points or fund prizes.

00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:34.086
Second are competition points, granted free only for answering sponsor advertising quizzes.

00:00:34.116 --> 00:00:38.779
Prize money comes only from sponsors and remains separate from company revenue.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.747
Competition points are not sold or bundled with any purchase.

00:00:42.777 --> 00:00:47.577
Users cannot transfer them to another person or move them outside the platform.

00:00:47.607 --> 00:00:51.469
They cannot be exchanged for cash, crypto, or external points.

00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:57.304
These limits reduce risk, but the actual screens, terms, and operation still require legal review.

00:00:57.404 --> 00:01:02.447
The initial support pieces are commemorative items, separate from future officially licensed cards.

00:01:02.477 --> 00:01:07.134
The center space starts visible, and supporters collect the surrounding eight pieces.

00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:12.208
Completing the image gives no points, level, tournament access, cash value, or prize.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:17.607
Before launch, we will disclose price, quantity, odds, duplicate rules, and end-of-service terms.

00:01:17.637 --> 00:01:20.757
We use only materials approved for digital use.

00:01:20.857 --> 00:01:25.512
In the knowledge competition, users allocate free points and answer anime questions.

00:01:25.542 --> 00:01:28.647
Sponsor contributions alone are planned to fund prizes.

00:01:28.677 --> 00:01:34.357
User payments, card sales, competition points, and company revenue do not enter the prize pool.

00:01:34.387 --> 00:01:40.588
Prize limits, age rules, identity checks, taxes, and delivery methods must be reviewed in each country.

00:01:40.688 --> 00:01:44.171
The initial prediction concept uses only non-cash competition points.

00:01:44.201 --> 00:01:49.247
Each question shows its official source, decision time, and invalidation rule before entry.

00:01:49.277 --> 00:01:52.237
No real-money version has been approved or scheduled.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:57.689
Any future version requires local review of gambling, finance, payments, identity, and tax rules.

00:01:57.789 --> 00:02:03.612
An official digital card requires a license that defines exactly what the company may offer.

00:02:03.642 --> 00:02:08.654
Paid secondary trading needs rights-holder consent and legal review in each launch country.

00:02:08.684 --> 00:02:11.789
Resale, liquidity, and price appreciation are not guaranteed.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:16.469
Advertising events and answers will be measured separately and explained to users.

00:02:16.499 --> 00:02:21.918
We plan to provide aggregated trends after user notice and consent, not personal histories.

00:02:22.018 --> 00:02:27.840
Before formal launch, external counsel must review the actual product, contracts, terms, and money flows.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.518
The review covers contests, payments, advertising law, privacy, finance, and IP rights.

00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:37.976
A feature will not launch until required licenses, registrations, and rights agreements are complete.

00:02:38.006 --> 00:02:41.088
We do not assume a simultaneous global launch.

00:02:41.188 --> 00:02:45.727
An external legal opinion cannot remove future regulatory or operational risk.

00:02:45.757 --> 00:02:51.572
We will keep the three flows separate, document actual operation, and review every material change.

00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:55.861
The principle is simple: offer only reviewed features, in reviewed countries.

00:02:55.891 --> 00:02:58.531
That is our plan for managing legal risk.
